How were you as a speaker in 2010?

00:23:46.839 --> 00:23:48.119
Do you think compared to now?

00:23:49.079 --> 00:23:50.040
Well, the video is online.

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:57.079
You can you can look and find out definitely less confident, less, you know, less practiced.

00:23:57.640 --> 00:24:03.640
I would say I, I still, I still, I see things that I did then that I still do now.

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:09.880
Like I, I'm prone to using a lot of filler words, like kind of, sort of, and, you know,

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:13.719
and those are, those are very difficult to get rid of, I find.

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:21.640
But I, yeah, since I'm more practiced and I've been been doing public speaking for the last

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:25.800
doing speaking 10 to 15 times a year for the last 15 years.

00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:29.239
So that's, that's a lot of public speaking engagements.

00:24:29.239 --> 00:24:34.599
And it definitely gets a little bit, a little bit easier, a lot less, a lot less nervous.

00:24:34.599 --> 00:24:40.040
I don't get as much of like the, the, the shakes, you know, like the stage fright that I used to,

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:44.199
like, I remember like back when I gave that talk, like, I remember the feeling of like my heart

00:24:44.199 --> 00:24:49.160
racing and like, you know, the judgment and like not knowing like how your content is going to land.

00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:54.119
And that's, that's very intimidating for a new, for a new speaker.

00:24:54.119 --> 00:24:59.400
And I think for, I think for some of us who give a lot of, who do a lot of public speaking it,

00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:04.280
after, after a while, after we've been doing it for such a long time, it can, we have to

00:25:04.280 --> 00:25:09.719
remind ourselves what it is like to be a first time, first time speaker to give your first or

00:25:09.719 --> 00:25:14.119
your first five public speaking engagements. It's, it's incredibly intimidating. And,

00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:21.000
and, you know, that's, I think that really needs to factor into like, you know, essentially helping,

00:25:21.079 --> 00:25:25.000
helping create more great, great public speakers for people to get their ideas out there.

