Yeah. So I did debate in high school, which is a little different to debate. It's English style

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:53.239
debate, which is a bit different to the American style. But I still remember, like, I think the

00:25:53.239 --> 00:26:02.040
thing that was, that really served me well from debate was like going to like, when you debate

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:10.359
at another school, you are talking in front of like an actively hostile audience. And like after

00:26:10.359 --> 00:26:14.359
that, like I've never had an actively, like I've had like, you know, you get passively hostile

00:26:14.359 --> 00:26:19.560
audiences or you get people who are like in the front row, just like staring at you grumpily,

00:26:19.560 --> 00:26:24.199
but there's like nothing going, nothing like going to another school that like wants you to lose.

00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:32.119
And I think that like, that prepared me fairly well. So everything after that was, was gravy.

00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:36.040
Yeah. Ruth, what was your first speech or talk?

