I remember for some reason in fourth grade, I ran for hall monitor and I had to give up,

00:26:43.400 --> 00:26:47.319
I had to get up and talk. And I just, like, I still remember being in the front of the classroom.

00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:52.280
I don't know. I guess it went well. I think I was elected. I didn't really run for anything else. I

00:26:52.280 --> 00:27:00.839
wasn't a great student, honestly. But I did a lot of activities in college that got me speaking,

00:27:00.839 --> 00:27:05.479
but I, my, my first real professional, I remember being nervous as hell.

00:27:06.119 --> 00:27:13.640
This is an odd way back machine, but in 1992, one of my first jobs, the whole packet to implement

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:18.680
national service landed on my desk. I was working in the governor's office. I was like a young,

00:27:18.680 --> 00:27:23.719
I was 25. And this guy in the office, like, this is your job, dropped it on me. So I had to

00:27:23.719 --> 00:27:29.959
implement national service in Ohio and write grants and recruit a staff and create a board

00:27:30.520 --> 00:27:36.520
and pass legislation. I had no business. I like, I had no experience in it, but that's what happens

00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:40.920
when you're young in politics. They just, you just keep going. And I had to do a bunch of like,

00:27:40.920 --> 00:27:46.680
really big speaking events when I was 25 around this, like with mayors and governor, you know,

00:27:46.680 --> 00:27:51.160
like announcing the launch of city year in Ohio and all of those kinds of things. And

00:27:52.520 --> 00:27:56.839
so that was my, yeah. But I'll, I think if you know my background, I spent most of my life

00:27:56.839 --> 00:28:04.040
listening to my father talk and he's dragged me to lectures and talks and salons. And so I

00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:10.599
forever was listening to talks. And that was a very common, comfortable thing. And at the dinner

00:28:10.599 --> 00:28:18.119
table, all we did was talk about ideas. It did, I mean, every night. So while it wasn't a first

00:28:18.119 --> 00:28:23.640
professional, I was constantly being asked to participate in those moments, which I think

00:28:24.599 --> 00:28:30.119
was a good breeding ground for this job. Do you feel like there was a moment where you knew

00:28:31.239 --> 00:28:37.800
like being a speaking coach and trainer was really the thing you wanted to do?

