I'll tell you exactly. I know exactly. There were two, one was when I was in college. Like I said,

00:28:43.479 --> 00:28:48.920
I didn't study a lot. I'm obviously not dumb, but like school wasn't like my thing.

00:28:49.239 --> 00:28:54.680
In my sophomore year, I took the first speaking class. It was like my first legitimate A in my

00:28:54.680 --> 00:29:00.280
life. And I was like, that was fun. And I want to do that. So that was my first. And then

00:29:01.400 --> 00:29:07.479
in 2009, when I did the first TEDx event, I did it because I was kind of bored in my PR practice.

00:29:07.479 --> 00:29:13.079
And I remember so vividly like the month after going home. And I tell this story sometimes

00:29:13.719 --> 00:29:19.719
sometimes thinking, why aren't you doing more of that? There were eight speakers on stage,

00:29:19.719 --> 00:29:23.800
including John Glenn, who was the astronaut. Again, did I have a license to be, you know,

00:29:23.800 --> 00:29:28.280
having him on my stage? Not really, but it's the way Columbus works because he lives here.

00:29:28.280 --> 00:29:34.040
He lived here. And it's why it's called John Glenn International Airport. If you ever fly

00:29:34.040 --> 00:29:39.479
into Columbus, he'll be there. But there were six people who did really well and two that kind of

00:29:39.479 --> 00:29:47.560
didn't. And I won't tell you who the two were that didn't. He was fine. But I remember one

00:29:47.560 --> 00:29:53.719
person showing up with like two full decks and she had 18 minutes. And I was like, what are you

00:29:53.719 --> 00:29:57.959
doing? Like, why don't you have one? Like, why are you two? She's like, I have two talks. This

00:29:57.959 --> 00:30:04.359
is the day before. And I was like, ah. And so I went to look for somebody to help me be a storytelling

00:30:04.359 --> 00:30:10.199
speaking coach for the next year, and I couldn't find anybody. I found like the media trainer types

00:30:10.199 --> 00:30:13.560
and then I found like the speech writers and I'd been a speech writer. And I was like, well,

00:30:13.560 --> 00:30:18.199
I guess I just have to figure this out on my own. So for the better part of a year, I just like

00:30:18.199 --> 00:30:24.119
studied. I read every book I could on directing and storytelling and structured thinking and

00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:30.520
speaking nonverbals, you name it. I mean, I had a library already from school, but I just really

00:30:30.520 --> 00:30:37.079
got myself really familiar with it. And then I had to learn training, which I didn't really know

00:30:37.079 --> 00:30:44.599
how to train or coach. And so I had to do that, too. And so by the end of 2010, I was done with

00:30:44.599 --> 00:30:52.359
the PR and the media and just started in kind of like kind of the snake that like leaves its skin.

00:30:52.359 --> 00:30:58.839
And so that was the start of it was for sure the TEDx event that kind of changed my perspective

00:30:58.839 --> 00:31:05.160
on it. And it's really interesting. It sounds like a lot of it started from trying to solve

00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:11.000
almost like a personal problem, like something you encountered and thought, like, there must be

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.280
someone who I could bring in and then.

00:31:14.778 --> 00:31:21.258
Like, there must be someone who I could bring in. And then that, like, curiosity, just to see,

00:31:21.258 --> 00:31:25.898
like, what would it take to fill that gap? Is all of all of you in the room or in some

00:31:25.898 --> 00:31:29.658
former fashion or entrepreneurs, you know, as you're starting up something, how they, I mean,

00:31:30.458 --> 00:31:33.497
that's what you do when you're an entrepreneur. You go look for the resource. Like, how,

00:31:33.497 --> 00:31:35.978
who's the per, who is the person that can help me? I just,

00:31:36.858 --> 00:31:40.858
at least the person didn't exist in Columbus. And there aren't many.

00:31:36.498 --> 00:31:45.178
I've been in proliferation now.

00:31:45.178 --> 00:31:50.138
TEDx has grown up a bunch of better storytelling coaches across the world.

